# FRONTEND DOCUMENTATION

## Project Name

Expense Tracker Frontend

---

## Project Overview

The Expense Tracker Frontend is developed using Streamlit. It provides a user-friendly interface for managing expenses and interacting with the FastAPI backend.

Users can:

* Add expenses
* View expenses
* Update expenses
* Delete expenses
* Analyze expense summaries

---

# Frontend Tech Stack

* Python
* Streamlit
* Pandas
* Requests

---

# Frontend Features

## Add Expense

Users can add:

* Title
* Amount
* Category
* Payment Method
* Expense Date
* Description

## View Expenses

Displays all expenses in table format.

## Update Expense

Users can update existing expense details.

## Delete Expense

Users can remove expenses using Expense ID.

## Expense Summary

Displays category-wise expense analysis using charts.

---

# Frontend Project Structure

```bash
frontend/
│
├── ft.py
├── requirements.txt
└── .streamlit/
    └── secrets.toml
```

---

# Frontend Installation

## Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone <repository_url>
```

---

## Step 2: Navigate to Frontend Folder

```bash
cd frontend
```

---

## Step 3: Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# Frontend requirements.txt

```txt
streamlit
requests
pandas
```

---

# Configure Backend URL

Create folder:

```bash
.streamlit
```

Create file:

```bash
.streamlit/secrets.toml
```

Add:

```toml
be_server_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
```

For deployed backend:

```toml
be_server_url = "https://your-backend-url.onrender.com"
```

---

# Run Frontend Locally

```bash
streamlit run ft.py
```

Frontend URL:

```bash
http://localhost:8501
```

---

# Frontend Deployment

## Deploy on Streamlit Cloud

### Deployment Steps

1. Push frontend code to GitHub
2. Open Streamlit Cloud
3. Connect GitHub repository
4. Select frontend/ft.py
5. Add secrets:

```toml
be_server_url = "https://your-backend-url.onrender.com"
```

6. Deploy application

---

# Frontend Workflow

```text
User → Streamlit Frontend → FastAPI Backend → MySQL Database
```

